package tv.nomercy.player.core.ports

// One video track and two audio tracks, English and Dutch, 320x180, 8 seconds.
//
// In commonTest so that every engine gate uses the same bytes. Media3 and
// AVFoundation reading the same file is the only way "both engines report two
// dubs" means anything — with a fixture each, a difference in the readings
// could always be a difference in the fixtures.
//
// Two audio tracks because one cannot tell a working switch from a no-op: with
// a single track, "select the other one" and "do nothing" read identically.
// The languages are the falsifiable part rather than the ids, which are
// positional and would look right even if the mapper read the wrong field.
//
// A base64 literal rather than a resource because there is no one way to ship a
// test resource across these targets: the Android KMP library plugin does not
// package assets for the device-test source set, and Kotlin/Native has no
// classpath to read one from.
//
// 320x180 rather than something smaller, and that is not arbitrary. The first
// version was 32x32 to keep the literal short, and a Sony Xperia refused it:
// "Decoder init failed, c2.qti.avc.decoder", an IllegalArgumentException out of
// MediaCodec.configure. Qualcomm's AVC decoder has a minimum frame size, and a
// clip below it never reaches READY — so all four gates failed on that phone as
// "the engine never reported metadata" while passing on the other two. The
// audio is 44.1kHz for the same class of reason: 8kHz is legal and not
// universally decodable.
